%% For H24_TorserCharts/PacketCharts copy the source body before standalone then;
%% replace the imported torsor theory by sort TR26Point and total tr26Translate.
%% Retain the actual packet free constructor/selectors. Add one original goal
%% per Focus as in the script. No group law is needed for these eight goals.
%% For AT26_ComplexReflectionReturns retain its two sorts, total comparison and
%% reflection operations, rh26OnLine, and exactly the source equations listed
%% above. Copy conjugation/flip axioms from RH26_DAGGER_ZERO_RETURN, excluding
%% its implied reflection goal. Both targets were proved directly.
%% 
%% CANCELLATION REPLAY BOUNDARY
%% Use the exact full AT26 bridge signature, retaining partial inverse/division,
%% power, Gamma and completion factor. Copy only the source laws shown per row.
%% C1 proves a+a=a=>a=0 using additive associativity, right identity and inverse.
%% C2 uses C1, distributivity and 0+0=0 to obtain x*0=0. C3 gives 1*x=x.
%% C4 is the H24 specified-left-inverse theorem in this exact typed signature.
%% C5 uses inverse domain/law and multiplication commutativity; C6 is its
%% nonzero-product consequence. C7 uses the explicit defined nonzero power/Gamma
%% imports and factor definition. C8 uses C7, C5 and continued completion.
%% C9 uses C5, the Mellin formula, and total halfShift=division(...,2), whose
%% division-domain law gives 2!=0. bridge_half_shift_source and bridge_mellin_source
%% name the actual unlabelled displayed source equations, not additional facts.
%% Every cut retains the predecessor formula including sort AND definedness
%% guards. Hets called MT26_R definedness gn_defined in a small signature but
%% gn_defined_1 in the full bridge. Regenerating all scalar cuts in the full
%% signature and checking each arg_restriction_gn_defined* equation fixed this
%% boundary; all nine nodes then proved at the same 3-second limit. Earlier
%% ResourceOut attempts are superseded; no target theorem was assumed.
%% 
%% OLD NINE-GOAL DAG (RECOVERY BEFORE DEDUPLICATION)
%% Historical receipts do not automatically certify a later renamed view.
%% Let F=Fix, S=Stab, c=S F. Fixed triple uses the two polar definitions and
%% subfield extensionality; stabilizer triple uses subgroup extensionality.
%% Closure composes the proved stabilizer triple at F(H) with c=S F.
%% No field/group operations, topology or choice. For x+y on the Boolean carrier:
%%  L0: 0+x=(x+x)+x=x+(x+x)=x;
%%  LR: x+(x+y)=(x+x)+y=y; RR: (x+y)+y=x+(y+y)=x.
%% These three scalar lemmas use associativity, right identity and self-inverse.
%% Each of four P_i: pi_i(Translate(p,w))=pi_i(p)+pi_i(w) is source-proved
%% from translation and beta. EXT follows from product eta.
%%  involution <- RR, four P_i, EXT; transporter <- LR, four P_i, EXT,
%%  Difference=Translate; unique transporter <- proved transporter, same definition.
%%  identity <- right identity, Origin=Point(0,0,0,0), translation, beta/eta.
%%  sigma unit <- pull, existential-image, pointwise-order definitions; witness x.
%%  tail step <- branch beta, Build/Run Cons equations, TailReturnAt definition:
%%  Run(b::w,Build(b::w,x))=Run(w,T(B_b(Build(w,x))))=Run(w,Build(w,x))=x.
%% All words additionally require structural induction. These are 9 targets plus
%% 3 scalar/4 projection/EXT helpers = 17 nodes. Exact guarded cuts, an acyclic
%% dependency graph and all predecessor proofs were audited. No vertex enumeration
%% or primitive commutativity was used.
%% 
%% SUPPORT LIMITS AND RECORD IDENTITIES
%% Middle-chart cancellation uses only Y section and three sharp definitions.
%% Fixed-point reflection uses only section and intertwining. The right-triple
%% E proof takes an opposite-poset detour, so its used set is not globally minimal.
%% MT26_f2_S and rh26_lagarias_at_one remain open in the old native ATP runs;
%% their existing exact symbolic/arithmetic checks are separate evidence.
%% Below SHA256 hashes identify canonical historical proof bundles: concatenate
%% goal + newline + complete TSTP proof in lexicographic goal order. New paths
%% or prover versions may change proof bytes. Hashes alone are not proofs.
%% core18 48035e833c97d3952256a56cd9783c5de4010df2a93f3bebc7da5789fe4bf84c
%% joined10 3b9f324632ad0d05fbd31dfdf4a682c423543a4f5f2dfa35eb14f3944ef81301
%% cancellation9 71c1a7696744c8ba9235fcd2bf515e7980b9459865ab2d44f2f0d36de7aa22f4

