%% BEGIN_PARACOLLATZ_CONSTRUCTIVE_PROOFS
%% 1. EXACT CARRIERS AND ASSUMPTIONS
%%
%% Write A for PN25Scalar and V=A^6 for PN25Six. The six raw coordinates are
%% (tau,b,L00,L01,L10,L11), in that order. The existing MT26 ring, explicit matrix
%% constructors, Gram matrix, and third are reused by a CASL sort renaming:
%% MT26_R -> PN25Scalar, V6 -> PN25Six, V4 -> PN25Four, M4 -> PN25Matrix.
%% The inherited operation names are overloaded on these renamed carriers.
%%
%% No characteristic-zero, field, order, completeness, prime conjecture, or
%% choice axiom is required for the algebra. The actual imported matrix instance
%% has 3 invertible. The cyclic normalization additionally supplies 63 invertible.
%% Since 63=3*21, the latter already forces 3 invertible in a commutative ring.
%% The dagger-only resolvent requires just 3 invertible. The carry equations and
%% finite geometric identities are integral identities; their mathematical
%% proofs work over any commutative ring/module even though the reused source
%% instance carries the harmless additional third.
%%
%% PN25Scalar must remain distinct from the complex field. Defining v~_m w by
%% v-w in 2^m A^6 and imposing separation on a field containing 1/2 would force
%% all points equal. The separated extension is instead an optional dyadic
%% instance, satisfied by Z[1/63], Z_2, and their appropriate separated modules.
%% Finite residue rings also satisfy separation, because sufficiently high
%% powers of 2 vanish; their points are residue classes, not full Z_2 integers.
%% The intended Z_2 instance supplies that carrier separately. Every finite cut
%% is retained; no fixed precision header is substituted for the full point.
%%
%% 2. ACTUAL SIX-CHANNEL CYCLE AND ITS INVERSE
%%
%% Define U(a,b,c,d,e,f)=(b,c,d,e,f,a), D=U^3, R=I-2U,
%% K=I+2U+4U^2, H=-(I+8U^3)/63, and N=K H. Coordinate substitution gives U^6=I,
%% D^2=I and the linearity of U. Multiply the degree-three polynomials:
%%
%%   (I-2U)(I+2U+4U^2)=I-8U^3,
%%   (I-8U^3)(I+8U^3)=I-64U^6=-63I.
%%
%% All factors are polynomials in the same U and commute. Multiplication by the
%% supplied inverse of 63 gives RN=NR=I. Expanding K H gives exactly
%%
%%   N=-(I+2U+4U^2+8U^3+16U^4+32U^5)/63.
%%
%% This proves both return clauses, the linearity of N, and uniqueness: if Rw=v,
%% then w=NRw=Nv. No series convergence is needed for this construction. The
%% rational/complex half-projectors (I+D)/2 and (I-D)/2 can interpret the source
%% spectral calculation, but are not operations in the dyadic construction.
%% Their combined resolvent has only the odd denominator 63.
%%
%% U^3 is this coordinate-cycle involution. It is not an order-six element of S3,
%% and it is not the native Gram dagger in Section 4. No such identification is
%% used by the formal fragment.
%%
%% 3. ORIGINAL FOUR-PORT RETURN AND NATURALITY
%%
%% Let w=(0,0,1,1,1,1)^T and ell(v)=L00+L01+L10+L11. Then Q(v)=ell(v)w is the
%% actual ordered source-port contraction. Its normalized action is Q_N=NQR.
%% By N's linearity, Q_N(v)=ell(Rv)Nw, so it is the stated rank-one row/column
%% factorization. The original-source return is a literal cancellation:
%%
%%   R Q_N N v = R N Q R N v = Qv.
%%
%% It retains each source mark and its multiplicity. Any later Boolean,
%% availability, or tropical projection must follow this signed original
%% readback; it is not applied between rational normalization factors.
%%
%% For an arbitrary supplied operation F_a:V->V define F'_a=N F_a R. Then
%% F'_a N=N F_a and R F'_a N=F_a, solely from RN=NR=I. This works for arbitrary
%% F_a, including nonlinear operations, because it is conjugation; it does not
%% claim that every operation commutes with U or with the Gram dagger. This is
%% the pair of PN25_Naturality goals and the H24_Retraction view. For a map of
%% coefficient rings preserving unit, every displayed polynomial expression is
%% preserved; the image of inv63 is the inverse of 63 by the unit equation.
%% Consequently coefficientwise scalar transport commutes with N as well.
%%
%% 4. THE SAME SPARSE FOUR-BY-FOUR MATRIX AND TRUE GRAM DAGGER
%%
%% The archived matrix is
%%   rho(tau,b,L) = [[tau-2b,0,0,0],[0,L00,L01,0],
%%                   [0,L10,L11,0],[b,0,0,tau]].
%% The current regular block is diag([[u,v],[v,u]],L), with u=tau-b and v=b.
%% The explicit integral J and J^-1 in PN25_NativeChart satisfy both inverse
%% products and rho=J block J^-1. These are unimodular changes of basis; no
%% inverse of 2 is introduced. The raw-channel decoder reads tau=a+b, b=b and
%% the four lower block entries, so decode(matrix(v))=v for every v. Raw native
%% channel coordinates and S3 group-algebra coefficients share a six-coordinate
%% carrier but retain their different named encoders and coordinate meanings.
%%
%% With Q4=diag(I2,[[2,-1],[-1,2]]), the actual native involution is
%% G(v)=decode(Q4^-1 matrix(v)^T Q4). The regular C2 block is symmetric, so it is
%% fixed; the lower 2x2 block is closed under this operation. Thus encoding Gv
%% is exactly dagger(encoding v). Since Q4 and Q4^-1 are symmetric, applying the
%% dagger twice returns the matrix; the explicit decoder returns G^2v=v.
%% The coordinate matrix of G is in the embedded PN25 algebra receipt and has denominator 3.
%% The recovered SemMatrixData source explicitly uses archived Gram matrix
%% [[1,0,0,1],[0,2,-1,0],[0,-1,2,0],[1,0,0,2]]. This is exactly
%% J^(-T) Q4 J^(-1), as the displayed J inverse shows by four column pairings.
%% Consequently the archived dagger is the conjugate of this same current
%% dagger; the name "actual Gram" is tied to the recovered source metric, not
%% merely to an arbitrary involution chosen for the new chart.
%%
%% Set L=I-2G and S=-(I+2G)/3. Then
%%   LS=SL=-(I-4G^2)/3=I.
%% For residual_b(v)=Lv-b and restore_b(r)=S(r+b), direct cancellation gives
%% restore_b(residual_b(v))=v and residual_b(restore_b(r))=r. Hence
%% residual_b(v)=0 iff v=restore_b(0), giving the constructed unique zero return.
%% This is an affine original-source inverse, with the actual dagger preserved.
%%
%% 5. EVERY DYADIC CUT AND THE ALREADY CONSTRUCTED FULL POINT
%%
%% Put s_m(v)=sum_{i<m}2^i U^i v, defined by s_0=0 and s_(m+1)=v+2Us_m.
%% Induct on m: the base R s_0=0=v-v holds. Applying R to the successor and
%% using commutation with U gives
%%   R s_(m+1)=Rv+2U R s_m
%%            =(v-2Uv)+2U(v-2^m U^m v)
%%            =v-2^(m+1)U^(m+1)v.
%% Thus, after applying N,
%%   s_m(v)-Nv = -2^m N U^m v.
%% The displayed right-hand side is an explicit ideal-membership witness for
%% s_m(v)~_m Nv. If v-w=2^m q, N(v)-N(w)=2^m Nq. Conversely, an ideal witness
%% for N(v)-N(w) is returned by R. Therefore N preserves AND reflects each cut.
%%
%% For m<=n, natural induction supplies n=m+k and 2^n=2^m 2^k; multiplying the
%% witness by 2^k restricts a congruence to the lower cut. Apply this to the two
%% congruences s_n(v)~_n Nv and s_m(v)~_m Nv, using transitivity, to obtain
%% s_n(v)~_m s_m(v). The normalized prefixes are a compatible inverse system.
%%
%% N(v) has already been exhibited by a finite algebraic formula. In a separated
%% dyadic instance, if w~_m s_m(v) for every m, then w~_m Nv for every m and
%% separation gives w=Nv. No general inverse-limit completeness or selection
%% principle is needed merely to exhibit this particular full point. Existence
%% of every arbitrary compatible family would be a different completeness
%% statement and is not asserted here.
%%
%% 6. THE ACTUAL CAUSAL BIT PRODUCER AND ITS CLOSED-FORM RETURN
%%
%% The embedded normalizer replay constructs six full adders for each bit column.
%% Let x_i,y_i,c_i,p_i be its input, output, carry and previous-output vectors,
%% with p_0=c_0=0 and p_(i+1)=y_i. In lane j the full adder evaluates
%%   t=x_(j,i)+p_((j+1) mod 6,i)+c_(j,i),
%%   y_(j,i)=t mod 2,  c_(j,i+1)=floor(t/2).
%% All three summands are bits, so t<=3 and the next carry is a bit. The exact
%% local equation is y_i=x_i+U p_i+c_i-2c_(i+1). The symbolic Boolean certificate
%% uses XOR(a,b)=a+b-2ab and bit idempotence, rather than a truth table.
%%
%% Define X_m=sum_(i<m)2^i x_i and Y_m=sum_(i<m)2^i y_i. Induction proves
%%   X_m-RY_m=2^m(c_m+U p_m).
%% The base is zero. At the successor, add 2^m(x_m-y_m+2Uy_m) to the old
%% invariant, substitute the full-adder equation, and cancel c_m+U p_m.
%% The result is 2^(m+1)(c_(m+1)+U y_m), as required. Applying N gives
%%   N X_m=Y_m+2^m N(c_m+U p_m).
%% Thus the executable producer returns exactly the archived closed normalizer
%% modulo 2^m, for every supplied prefix and every m. Its earlier digits are
%% independent of later inputs, so successive cuts commute. PN25_DigitProducer
%% records the local arithmetic transition and the three derived return goals;
%% the actual bit constraint and fixed reversible implementation are supplied by
%% the executable compiler, not by an assumed global answer equation.
%%
%% 7. RETAINED BASE-3/2 CARRIES, INCLUDING PADDING AND INVERSE WORD
%%
%% For a tape of length d define the homogeneous numerator
%%   H([])=0,  H(a::t)=a*2^length(t)+3H(t).
%% For d>0 its rational weighted value is H/2^(d-1). This integer polynomial is
%% usable inside the dyadic ring; 3/2 itself is not a dyadic integer.
%%
%% At address zero with at least two cells the actual move is
%% (a,b)->(a-3q,b+2q). Replacing q by -q restores both cells. For a tail of length
%% k, the numerator difference is
%%   (-3q)*2^(k+1)+3*(2q)*2^k=0.
%% Length is unchanged. An address beyond the last adjacent pair is the original
%% defined no-op. For a positive address, recurse through the retained head;
%% structural induction on tape/address proves inverse, length and numerator
%% preservation in every case. No padding is trimmed or regenerated.
%%
%% The actual word action applies the head move and then the remaining word.
%% Its inverse reverses the order and negates each q. The shared H24 fold-append
%% fusion law makes run(u++v,t)=run(v,run(u,t)). Induct on u, use the local inverse,
%% and apply the induction hypothesis to obtain BOTH whole-word return equations.
%% The same induction composes numerator and extent invariance. Keeping the
%% original coefficient sign and odd denominator outside the transformed tape
%% therefore returns the same rational coefficient. The live readback evaluates
%% the normalized tape; it need not substitute the original numerator.
%% END_PARACOLLATZ_CONSTRUCTIVE_PROOFS

%% BEGIN_NORMALIZER_REPLAY_PY
%% #!/usr/bin/env python3
